Z||000000||BAM-BAM||08-20-2000||11:39 AM||||  Sorry to say that I will be retiring from Fierodom for a while. On my way home from work yesterday I was broadsided by a guy in a DaeWoo Leganza making a U-Turn from the shoulder of the road. It's hard to tell the extent of the damages untill the panels come off, however my right rear wheel has about a fifteen degree toe in and my rear end tracks the front about 8 inches to the left. I had just gotten the alignment problems worked out and had been driving the car for four days since the new suspension. What a difference that suspension makes. Well, I'll check in from time to time and I'll be back full time when and if I get another Fiero. Look for me on the Mall, I may be having parts for sale <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||9
Z||000001||RobertVol||08-20-2000||12:32 PM||||BAM SORRY TO HEAR THAT !!!!<P>I would be thinking man couldnt something else hit me like a Firebird or a Pick up Truck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>A DAEWOO !?!?!? What the pluck? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>man sorry about that. Hope you get back soon ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||08-20-2000||12:41 PM||||Damn, that just sucks.  If any good is to be said, it's that it was obviously his fault, and it being a new car, it should be fully insured. I hope you get back into the plastic soon.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Big O||08-20-2000||06:25 PM||||Man, after all that work to get your suspension straightened out and some dipstick has to go and rearrange it for you.  What did you finally have to do to get the alignment done.  Did the info I sent you help?  Did you go back to the local Big O to get it done?  If you are interested in a really cherry 84 2M4 the owner of Rare Parts has one up for sale.  It needs some minor interior work on the door panels but other than that and some light scratches in the paint it looks beautiful.  Anyone out there interested can get in touch with me.  Rare parts is a company in Stockton that sells suspension components for all American made cars from the 30's to the present.  This guy got his Fiero and was in the process of completely restoring it when he lost interest.  It does look really nice though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||08-20-2000||08:56 PM||||  Big O, No, I didn't take it back to BIG-O. Instead, I took it to where all the racers take their cars. It's a little shop tucked in a hole. They used a caster kit and set everything per your (and others) settings, it came out great. They settled on 5.5* of positive caster on both sides. Everything else was set to your specs. I was enjoying the new performance alot. It makes a world of difference. I guess tomorrow I'll find out more about what they will do for me. The guy was driving a rental car but said his insurance was in effect, so, we'll see. Who knows maybe they will pay me replacement cost and let me buy mine back cheap. That way I can change over the suspension to what ever I buy. Then I'll part out the rest.<BR>Anyway, only time will tell. Thanks for everyones help along the way and look for me in a few weeks. Be good and thanks again.<P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
